0 @N4191@ NOTE <p>DF</p><p><p>Notes for PATRICK (PAT DONIE) FRIEL:</p></p><p><p>Pa
1 CONC t is recorded in both the 1901 and 1911 Census. He moved to live in McCo
1 CONC nigley's in Ballure when he married Maryanne, one of the three McConigle
1 CONC y sisters - Bridget and Sally being the others. He rebuilt the McConigle
1 CONC y house in 1932, and continued to live there until his death in 1980. H
1 CONC e was a small stocky man with a limp, relatively quiet, and always givin
1 CONC g the impression of being at ease with himself and the world. Dad freque
1 CONC ntly mentioned that he had worked as a "sapper" - possibly working for t
1 CONC he Ordnance Survey and working as far away as Tyrone. In latter years, h
1 CONC e would sit for long periods at the turf fire in the house in Ballure, s
1 CONC moking his pipe and spitting occasionally into the flames. He survived t
1 CONC he amputation of one of his legs in his early 90's, and was confined t
1 CONC o a wheelchair thereafter.</p><p></p>
