0 @N4193@ NOTE <p>DF</p><p><p>Notes for MARY (PAT) FRIEL:</p></p><p><p>Mary was th
1 CONC e eldest of the family. Dad remembers her as being frequently unwell - q
1 CONC uery if she contacted TB. (Note Sept 2007 - Peggy stated that Mary had h
1 CONC ad polio and that she had a small limp as a consequence.) She was looke
1 CONC d after by nuns, possibly in Derry, for a period but they did not keep h
1 CONC er - she may have gone to join them but may have been rejected on healt
1 CONC h grounds. Dad says that she as quiet and had lovely long brown hair, th
1 CONC ough she also had lumps on her wrist and on the back of her knee which h
1 CONC e wondered might be realted to her illness - which he also suggested mig
1 CONC ht have been cancer-related. She was unmarried. There is some confusio
1 CONC n re her age, though it is given on her grave in Massmount as 23 when sh
1 CONC e died. Her date of birth is noted as April 1913 in the Ballymichael Sch
1 CONC ool records.</p><p></p>
